  <ferc:DisclosureOfRespondentAppearingInAnnualReportToTheStockholdersTextBlock id="HH5E4D37729B3C0D95B1347B63AFD3C1FF" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:DisclosureOfRespondentAppearingInAnnualReportToTheStockholdersTextBlock>
  <ferc:FormType id="HHF7EC89F6B6814CD2CC1C6928B801FC93" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">6-Q</ferc:FormType>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="HHBD1AFC97EAE2BF213BAE5A53CD7CEAC7" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">Q1</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 12.0pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12.0pt 0in 12.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;Organization. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;NuStar Pipeline Operating Partnership L.P. ("NuPop") is a Delaware limited liability partnership which wholly owns Shore Terminal LLC, a Delaware limited liability company. NuPop also owns 99% of Cooperatie Nustar Holdings U.A., a Netherlands company.NuPop is owned 99% by NuStar Pipeline Partners L.P., and 1% by NuStar Pipeline Company, LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12.0pt 0in 12.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;Sunoco Midstream Merger. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;Effective July 1,2025, the membership interest in Shore Terminals LLC held by NuPop was transferred to Sunoco Midstream LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12.0pt 0in 12.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;Operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;NuPop owns pipeline systems that transport refined petroleum products, including gasoline, diesel, and propane throughout Kansas, Nebraska, Iowa, South Dakota, North Dakota, and Minnesota. In addition, NuPop operates an anhydrous ammonia pipeline system in Louisiana, Arkansas, Missouri, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa and Nebraska.Anhydrous ammonia is primarily used as agricultural fertilizer and used as a feedstock to a few industrial applications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12.0pt 0in 10.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;. NuPop's transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") and various federal and state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 10.0pt 0in 10.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;Basis of Presentation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP"). The most significant difference between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) subsidiaries are reflected on the equity method whereas GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated (2) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (3) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 10.0pt 0in 10.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;These interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes thereto contained in&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;the NuPop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#8217;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;FERC Form 6 for the year ended December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;. The financial statements are unaudited, but in the opinion of management, all adjustments have been made that are necessary to fairly state the financial position, results of operations and cash flows for the periods presented. Certain information and notes that would substantially duplicate the disclosures contained in the most recent FERC Form 6 have been omitted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 10.0pt 0in 10.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt;"&gt;NOTE B - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 12.0pt 0in 12.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of March 31,2026 and 2025 were $4.4 million and $4 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
